    {
      "name": "Realtime (WebSocket)",
      "description": "The WebSocket feed at `{{wsUrl}}` cannot be run from this collection:\nthe Postman v2.1.0 schema has no WebSocket request type, a collection holding\nWebSocket requests cannot also hold HTTP requests, and Newman cannot execute them.\nExercise it manually:\n\n### Connect\n\n1. **New → WebSocket Request**, enter `ws://localhost:8000/ws`, press **Connect**.\n2. The server immediately pushes `{ \"type\": \"welcome\" }`.\n\n### Subscribe to a match\n\nCommentary is delivered **only to subscribers of that match**. Send:\n\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"subscribe\", \"matchId\": 1 }\n```\n\nThe server replies `{ \"type\": \"subscribed\", \"matchId\": 1 }`.\n\nThen run **Commentary → POST /matches/:id/commentary** for that same match id.\nThe socket receives:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"commentary\",\n  \"data\": { \"id\": 1, \"matchId\": 1, \"sequence\": 1, \"eventType\": \"goal\", \"message\": \"Goal for Riffa!\", \"tags\": [\"goal\"] }\n}\n```\n\nSend `{ \"type\": \"unsubscribe\", \"matchId\": 1 }` to stop receiving them.\nClosing the socket unsubscribes from everything automatically.\n\n### Message reference\n\n**Client → server**\n\n| type | fields | notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `subscribe` | `matchId` | must be a positive integer |\n| `unsubscribe` | `matchId` | must be a positive integer |\n\n**Server → client**\n\n| type | when | payload |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `welcome` | on connect | none |\n| `subscribed` / `unsubscribed` | ack | `matchId` |\n| `error` | bad JSON or unsupported message | `message` |\n| `match_created` | after `POST /matches` | full match row (**all clients**) |\n| `commentary` | after `POST /matches/:id/commentary` | full commentary row (**subscribers only**) |\n\nMalformed input is answered with an `error` message and does not drop the connection.\nThe server pings every 30s and terminates sockets that stop responding.\nMax payload 1 MB; any path other than `/ws` is rejected with 404.",
      "item": []
    }
  ]
